// Figure 4.3 — Sequence diagram: an analyst reviews an alert
// Eraser: New diagram > Sequence diagram, paste this code.
title Review an alert

Analyst [icon: user, color: blue]
Browser [icon: monitor, color: orange]
Web server [icon: server, color: blue]
Inference service [icon: cpu, color: purple]
PostgreSQL [icon: database, color: green]

Analyst > Browser: open alert from list
Browser > Web server: GET /api/alerts/:id/explanation (session cookie)
activate Web server
Web server > PostgreSQL: verify session user, role, active
alt [label: explanation cached, color: green] {
  PostgreSQL --> Web server: stored attributions
}
else [label: first view] {
  Web server > Inference service: POST /explain (features)
  Inference service --> Web server: integrated-gradients attributions
  Web server > PostgreSQL: cache explanation (same model only)
}
Web server --> Browser: top features pushing toward fraud / legitimate
deactivate Web server

Analyst > Browser: Confirm fraud / Mark false positive + note
Browser > Web server: PATCH /api/alerts/:id decision and note
activate Web server
Web server > PostgreSQL: BEGIN; SELECT alert FOR UPDATE
alt [label: already reviewed and user is analyst, color: red] {
  Web server --> Browser: 403 Only an admin can change the decision
}
Web server > PostgreSQL: UPDATE alert; move daily_stats counters; INSERT audit_logs; COMMIT
Web server --> Browser: updated alert (and SSE to every open dashboard)
deactivate Web server
Browser --> Analyst: decision recorded
